'''tree-hoopoe''' (trē′hö″pō), ''n.'' nus ''Irrisor'' (which see, with cut). Also called ''wood-hoopoe.''

'''tree-hopper''' (trē′hop″ėr), ''n.'' Any one of a number of homopterous insects of the families ''Membracidæ'', ''Tettigoniidæ'', and ''Jassidæ'', which frequent trees or arborescent plants. {{smaller|''Ceresa bubalus'' is the buffalo tree-hop-}}
